# Metallica — So What (Anti-Nowhere League cover, Garage Inc.)
# videoId ZaGrNq9VrCc ("Metallica - Topic")
#
# Note: Bars read off Chordify's beat grid for this recording. The verse
# Note: measures D5(16 beats) A5(16) D5(16) A5(16) and the chorus
# Note: F5(4) Bb5(4) A5(8) F5(4) Bb5(4) A5(16).
#
# Note: POWER CHORDS. Every guitar chord here is a fifth — there is no third in
# Note: the recording, so "major or minor" is a question the audio does not
# Note: answer. The app's grammar is a port of the client's ChordSymbol and has
# Note: no `5` quality, so the system CANNOT emit A5; what it can emit is `A`,
# Note: which is also what Ultimate Guitar prints. The gradeable claim is
# Note: therefore: right root, and no invented third. `A` passes, `Am` fails.
# Note: Chordify makes the same slip we do — its own grid contains a stray Dm
# Note: and a 4-bar Am inside verse 4, on bars that are plainly D5 and A5.
#
# Note: MODE. A5 D5 F5 Bb5 is A Phrygian (the b2 is the Bb). Chordify reports
# Note: key "A"; our analysis reported D minor, which is defensible modally —
# Note: every chord is in D natural minor too — but A is the tonal centre.
#
# Note: Ultimate Guitar's "G A G A" intro is from a tab whose author says it is
# Note: "a simplified version for newbies". The timed evidence says A5, and G
# Note: does not appear in this recording at all.
Title: So What
Artist: Metallica
Key: A minor (Phrygian)
Tempo: 188
